('cat:swimming-pools','Regulations, licensing & approvals',8,'Governing legislation (per DM-HSD-GU34-ASPP2 V4.0, 4 May 2024): Local Order No. 61/1991 and Local Order No. 11/2003 on planning, building, maintenance and safety of swimming pools, administered by Dubai Municipality Health and Safety Department, Registration and Permits Section. Every pool in the Emirate of Dubai - including a private villa pool - must be registered/approved by DM before construction starts; building without DM approval is illegal. Submission is via the Dubai Building Permits System (Dubai BPS) for DM-authority areas, or via the relevant authority in gated/free zones (DDA, Trakhees/PCFC) where a developer/master-community NOC is a supporting document. Drawings are submitted electronically as a single multi-sheet DWF file including an owner-signed front page, site/setting-out plan, pool details (stairs, ladders, showers, toilets, lifeguard and lifebuoy positions, lighting, depth marks, fence, deck, slope), cross-section, pipe-fitting layout, electrical and schematic diagrams, water-drainage/backwash disposal scheme, and a pump-room layout with disinfection systems and water-turnover calculations. Parallel approvals are typically needed from DEWA (electrical and plumbing/water), Dubai Civil Defence (fire/safety, plant-room electrical for larger/public pools) and DM Drainage and Irrigation. The contractor must hold a valid DED trade licence whose activity covers swimming pool construction - ''DM-approved contractor'' is a marketing claim; the binding requirement is the licensed activity plus per-project DM plan approval. Private vs public differences (GU34): deck clearance >=1.0 m (private) vs >=1.5 m (public); filters 1 (private) vs 2 (public); automatic dosing mandatory for public (manual not accepted); lifeguard high-chair for hotels/schools/clubs; microbiological testing every 2 months for public (Trakhees LD-RC-G10). Safety: perimeter barrier >=1.20 m with a self-closing self-latching gate opening outward; kids'' pool barrier 1.2 m; bilingual ''No Diving'' signage. Indicative approval timeline up to ~6 weeks (secondary).'),
('cat:aluminium-glass','Authoritative sources & references',4,'Dubai Municipality (Building Permits / Al Sa''fat) — https://www.dm.gov.ae/
Al Sa''fat Dubai Green Building Evaluation System — https://www.dm.gov.ae/municipality-business/al-safat-dubai-green-building/
