('cat:ac-maintenance','Customer intake & scoping questions',9,'1. Property type (apartment, villa, office, retail, warehouse) and number of AC units? 2. Unit type per system: window, split, ducted/concealed split, cassette, package, or central/chiller? 3. Tonnage/BTU of each unit (or rooms covered) if known? 4. Is this a one-time service, breakdown repair, or annual maintenance contract (AMC)? 5. What symptoms — not cooling, water leak, noise, smell, tripping, high bill? 6. Brand and approximate age of units (Daikin, LG, Gree, Carrier, O General, etc.)? 7. Refrigerant type if known (R410A or R32)? 8. For AMC: how many preventive visits per year do you want, and should gas top-up, consumables and minor parts be included? 9. Are spare parts (compressor, fan motor, PCB) and refrigerant in or out of scope? 10. Access details (roof units, height, occupied premises, working hours)? 11. Is duct cleaning also required? 12. Warranty status of units (still under manufacturer warranty)? 13. Timeline/urgency? 14. Budget or preference for one-off vs contract?'),
('cat:swimming-pools','Authoritative sources & references',4,'Dubai Municipality Technical Guidelines for Approval of Swimming Pool Plans DM-HSD-GU34-ASPP2 V4.0 (official PDF, core technical figures) — https://www.dm.gov.ae/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/DM-HSD-GU34-ASPP2_Technical-Guidelines-for-Approval-of-Swimming-Pool-Plans_V4.pdf
