Signtrade (ACP material reference) — https://signtrade.com/product/aluminum-composite-panel-acp-sheet/'),
('cat:waterproofing','Customer intake & scoping questions',9,'1. Which substrates/zones need waterproofing - roof, podium deck, basement raft/retaining wall, bathroom/wet area, kitchen/laundry, water tank (potable?), pool, planter/landscape, balcony/terrace? Each has a different correct system. 2. New construction, refurbishment, or active-leak remediation (remediation needs leak diagnosis first)? 3. Total area per zone (m2) and number of penetrations (drains, pipes, anchors)? 4. Is this in a developer-managed community (Emaar, Nakheel), a free zone (DDA/Trakhees/TECOM) or standard DM jurisdiction? Determines whose NOC/fit-out approval and material spec applies. 5. Is a DM fit-out permit or developer NOC required (any wet-area relocation/MEP change typically triggers it)? 6. Is DCL-certified material mandated by the consultant/developer, and a specific approved brand/system? 7. What warranty is required - is 10-year full-system coverage specified? 8. Exposed or covered system (exposed roof PU needs a UV-stable aliphatic topcoat; buried needs protection screed/board)? 9. Substrate condition: existing cracks, dampness, prior failed membrane to remove, structural movement, negative-side water pressure? 10. Groundwater/high water table for basement tanking (Dubai coastal areas have aggressive saline groundwater), and is there a soil/groundwater report? 11. Required service life and budget tier (economy bitumen vs premium PU/sheet)? 12. Access and scheduling: occupied building, work at height, confined space (tanks/lift pits), traffic over podium needing a trafficable system? 13. Will a flood/ponding test be permitted and witnessed, and who signs off? 14. Will the contractor provide system data sheets, MSDS, DCL/conformity certificate and a method statement for approval before starting?'),
('cat:aluminium-glass','Quote analysis & comparison',9,'A complete aluminium & glass quote lists, per item: system/profile (alloy 6063-T5/T6, series/depth), finish (powder-coat to AAMA/Qualicoat or anodised, colour, microns), glass make-up, hardware/accessories brand, gaskets/sealant (structural vs weather silicone), thermal break (polyamide) yes/no, fabrication, transport, supply & install, scaffold/access, and warranty. The spec parameters that differentiate quotes (always with units): glass thickness (e.g. 6/8/10/12mm), single vs double glazing/IGU make-up (e.g. 6mm + 12mm air/argon + 6mm), tempered vs laminated (PVB 0.38/0.76/1.52mm), Low-E coating, U-value (W/m2K, e.g. 1.2-1.8 for good IGU) and SHGC, profile wall thickness (mm), with/without thermal break. A strong quote names brands, microns, U-value and thermal break; an underpriced one cuts corners by quietly substituting single glazing for double, thinner glass (e.g. 5mm where 8mm tempered is needed), removing the thermal break, thinner non-rated profiles, generic gaskets/sealant, or annealed glass where tempered/laminated safety glass is mandatory. Highlight to customers comparing 2-3 quotes: glazing type, U-value, thermal break, glass safety rating, finish microns, and warranty length. Common tricks: supply-only quoted as if installed, excluded DCD/DM fees and structural-glazing test certificates, VAT 5% excluded, scaffolding/crane excluded, off-brand profile substitution, vague ''as per drawing'' scope.'),
('cat:false-ceiling','Authoritative sources & references',4,'Dubai Municipality (Building Permits / fit-out) — https://www.dm.gov.ae/
