('cat:handyman','Authoritative sources & references',4,'Dubai Department of Economy and Tourism (trade licensing) - https://www.dubaided.gov.ae/en
Dubai Municipality (building maintenance / environmental approvals) - https://www.dm.gov.ae/
DEWA - registered electrical contractors and regulations - https://www.dewa.gov.ae/en/consumer/building-services/registered-contractors
DEWA - Green Building / energy and AC guidance - https://www.dewa.gov.ae/en
UAE Fire and Life Safety Code of Practice (Dubai Civil Defence) - https://www.dcd.gov.ae/portal/en/preventive-safety/rules-regulations/uae-fire-and-life-safety-code-of-practice.jsp
MOHRE (labour/visa compliance for technicians) - https://www.mohre.gov.ae/en/home.aspx
Dubai REST / Dubai Land Department (Ejari, owners associations) - https://dubailand.gov.ae/en/
Starting a building maintenance company in Dubai (licence guidance) - https://paramountzone.ae/blog/start-a-building-maintenance-company-dubai/
AMC contract scope reference (residential AMC) - https://www.wewillfixit.com/annual-contract/residential/
AC AMC scope and value guidance - https://geem.com/blog/ac-annual-maintenance-contract-dubai'),
('cat:movers','Pricing benchmarks & red flags',7,'Indicative Dubai pricing (verify; varies by volume, distance, access, season): local apartment moves are commonly priced by size - e.g. studio/1BR at the lower end and larger villas substantially higher - with full-pack, dismantle/reassemble, crew and truck bundled. Drivers: volume (CBM/rooms), crew size and truck size/trips, floor and lift access (stairs and long carry add cost), packing level and materials, insurance coverage, storage duration, special items (piano/safe/marble), distance/inter-emirate, and peak-season/end-of-month demand. Red flags: a low ''from AED X'' with no survey or inventory (almost always rises on the day); undersized crew/truck leading to extra-trip surcharges; ''packing included'' meaning labour only with materials billed separately; no insurance or only a nominal liability cap (e.g. a few dirhams per kg); no DET licence or no RTA goods-transport permit; freelance/unsponsored crew; cash-only with no written inventory or contract; excluded building move-in deposit/permit and gate-pass costs; and missing 5% VAT. A trustworthy quote is survey-based and fixed, names crew/truck, lists materials, and states insurance type and coverage limit in writing.'),
('_global','Asset text: README.txt',45,'From company asset "README.txt" (Dropbox: /QuotesDone Backup/Assets/README.txt)

QuotesDone — Company Assets folder
==================================

Drop company assets here and they auto-sync into every AI agent''s knowledge
(usually within the hour). Agents become aware of what exists and, for text
files, can read the contents.

What to put here:
- PRO brand kit (logo files, colour codes, fonts)  -> .pdf / .png / .svg / .zip
- Social media kit (templates, post specs, hashtags) -> .pdf / .png / .zip
- Brand voice / messaging guides                    -> .md / .txt  (agents read these fully)
- Lead lists                                        -> .csv / .xlsx (indexed; agents know they exist)
- Any reference doc you want agents to know about   -> .md / .txt preferred

Notes:
- Text files (.md .txt .csv .json .html) under 200 KB are read into agent knowledge in full.
- Images, PDFs, zips and spreadsheets are INDEXED (name, type, size, Dropbox path) so
  agents know they exist and can point you to them, but their contents are not pasted in.
- Remove a file here and it disappears from agent knowledge on the next sync.
'),
('cat:plumbing','Regulations, licensing & approvals',8,'Two authorities matter. The Dubai Electricity and Water Authority (DEWA) governs the water supply from the city main to the property meter: works on the connection, metering or supply require DEWA-approved contractors and DEWA approval/No Objection Certificate (NOC) before starting. Dubai Municipality (DM) sets the building codes governing plumbing and drainage inside the property line, through the Dubai Building Code and the Green Building Regulations & Specifications (which mandate water-efficient/low-flow fixtures, and in larger developments greywater and rainwater systems). The company must hold a Dubai Department of Economy and Tourism (DET/DED) trade licence for plumbing/MEP, and plumbers should be competent and, for supply-side work, DEWA-approved. Typical workflow for notable works: obtain DEWA NOC/approval (and DM approval for fit-outs/MEP), execute with licensed personnel, carry out pressure testing to check for leaks, then a final authority check before commissioning/sign-off. Minor like-for-like repairs inside a unit usually do not need authority approval, but works affecting the meter, main lines, common drainage or building structure typically do, and owner-association/building NOCs may also be required. Always confirm the contractor''s licence covers plumbing and that DEWA approval responsibility is clear in the quote.'),
('cat:curtains-blinds','Customer intake & scoping questions',9,'Ask: (1) How many windows/openings, and the width x height of each (mm)? Can you share a measurement sheet or photos? (2) Product type wanted per window - curtains (wave, pinch pleat, eyelet) or blinds (roller, zebra, roman, venetian, honeycomb)? (3) Light control needed - 100% blackout (bedrooms), dimout, sheer/day-night, or sun/heat-reflective? (4) Manual or motorised? If motorised, do you want a specific brand (Somfy) and control by remote, wall switch, or smart app (Alexa/Google/HomeKit)? (5) Property type and status - villa, apartment, hotel, office, retail; new build or replacement (need old curtains removed)? (6) Any double-height, bay, curved, or skylight windows needing scaffolding or curved track? (7) Fabric preference - colour, pattern, blockout, and any fire-retardant (FR) requirement for hotels/offices/malls (NFPA 701 / BS 5867)? (8) Is there power near the windows for wired motors, or is battery/solar needed? (9) Style references or budget range per window or total? (10) Timeline / move-in or handover date? (11) Is this a tenant (landlord NOC needed for drilling) or owner? (12) Do you need site measurement visit, or will you provide sizes? (13) Quantity of identical units (for pricing breaks)? (14) Warranty expectation on fabric and motor?'),
('cat:landscaping','Quote analysis & comparison',9,'A complete landscaping quote separates softscape and hardscape and itemises each. Softscape: lawn (natural turf vs artificial grass with gsm/pile height), soil/topsoil supply and depth, plants/shrubs/trees by species, size/grade (pot size or height) and quantity, ground cover, mulch/gravel, green/vertical walls. Hardscape: paving (interlock vs natural stone, area sqm, sub-base), pergola/gazebo (size, material - aluminium/wood/WPC, wind-load), decking, water feature/pool coping, boundary/retaining walls, outdoor lighting (fixtures, transformer), drainage. Irrigation: type (drip vs pop-up sprinkler/spray), zones/valves, controller (smart/Wi-Fi), backflow preventer, water source (mains/sweet water vs TSE treated sewage effluent), pipe runs. Also: site clearance/excavation, waste disposal, NOC/permit handling, maintenance period, warranty on plants and workmanship, and 5% VAT. Differentiators WITH units: softscape vs hardscape split (AED/sqm each), irrigation as drip vs sprinkler and zone count, plant grade/size, paving type, and whether TSE connection is included. Strong quote: line-by-line softscape/hardscape, named plant species and sizes, irrigation with backflow preventer and controller, plant-establishment warranty (e.g. 90 days), permits handled. Corner-cutting: a single AED/sqm blanket rate hiding cheap plants and no drainage; ''irrigation included'' that is bare drip with no controller/backflow; small immature plants priced as mature; no soil prep; excluded NOC/permit; no maintenance period. Highlight to customer: soft/hard split, plant sizes and warranty, irrigation completeness (backflow + controller + zones), drainage, and permit responsibility.'),
('cat:movers','Authoritative sources & references',4,'Roads and Transport Authority (RTA) Dubai - https://www.rta.ae/wps/portal/rta/ae/home
Dubai Department of Economy and Tourism (trade licensing) - https://www.dubaided.gov.ae/en
MOHRE (crew visa/labour compliance) - https://www.mohre.gov.ae/en/home.aspx
Dubai REST / Dubai Land Department (Ejari, community/building rules) - https://dubailand.gov.ae/en/
UAE Government portal - business licensing overview - https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/business
Start a transport company in Dubai - RTA approval and licence guide - https://diac.ae/blog/start-a-transport-company-in-dubai-uae/
RTA approval Dubai - licensing fees and process - https://dahhanbiz.com/roads-and-transport-authority-rta-approval/
Licensed vs unlicensed movers Dubai (how to verify) - https://movers-dubai.ae/blog/licensed-vs-unlicensed-movers-dubai
Logistics licence in Dubai step-by-step - https://www.retyn.ai/en-ae/blog/how-to-get-a-logistics-license-dubai
Professional movers and packers UAE (insurance/goods-in-transit reference) - https://www.trukker.com/home-moving'),
('_global','Asset text: brand-quick-reference.md',45,'From company asset "brand-quick-reference.md" (Dropbox: /QuotesDone Backup/Assets/brand-quick-reference.md)

# QuotesDone — Brand Quick Reference

**Name:** QuotesDone
**What it is:** UAE B2B anonymous quotation marketplace. Customers post a job; verified suppliers quote anonymously; the customer pays a small reveal fee only to unlock the supplier they choose.
**One-liner:** Get real quotes from verified UAE suppliers — anonymously, no spam, no haggling.

## Voice & tone
- Practical, trustworthy, pro-SME. Sound like a sharp operations manager, not a hype marketer.
- Short sentences. Concrete benefits. No invented statistics, no emojis in formal copy.
- Bilingual market: English + Modern Standard Arabic. Keep Arabic clean and professional.

## Core value props
1. Anonymous until you choose — suppliers never see who else quoted; you''re not swarmed by calls.
2. Verified suppliers only — trade licence + track record checked.
3. Pay only when you win — a 3% reveal fee on the quote you accept, nothing upfront.

## Do / Don''t
- DO lead with the customer''s problem, then the outcome.
- DO mention "verified UAE suppliers" and "anonymous" — they''re the differentiators.
- DON''T promise specific savings percentages or delivery times we can''t guarantee.
- DON''T imply suppliers pay commission on won jobs (they don''t).

## Contact
- Web: quotesdone.com  ·  Support: management@quotesdone.com  ·  Mobile/WhatsApp: +971 50 931 9355
'),
('_global','Asset text: WHERE_TO_USE.txt',45,'From company asset "WHERE_TO_USE.txt" (Dropbox: /QuotesDone Backup/Assets/QuotesDone_Brand_Kit/QuotesDone_Brand_Kit/WHERE_TO_USE.txt)

QUOTESDONE — BRAND KIT  ·  WHERE TO USE WHAT
============================================
Brand colours
  Teal  : #14B8A6  (gradient light #6EE7D4 → deep #0B8276)
  Gold  : #E3C065  (gradient #F6DD8C → #BD8E36)
  Navy  : #0C2330  (background gradient #173A4B → #06121B)
  Ink   : #0A0A0A  (one-colour / print)
Clear space: keep at least the height of the "Q" ring clear around the logo.
Smallest use: mark not below 24 px; full lockup not below 120 px wide.

01_Social_Avatars/   → Profile picture. Same square for every platform, pre-sized:
                       LinkedIn, Instagram, Facebook, X/Twitter, YouTube, WhatsApp,
                       TikTok, Threads, Pinterest, Google Business. Use the one
                       named for your platform; Universal_Master if unsure.

02_Social_Covers/    → Header / banner images:
                       LinkedIn personal 1584x396 · LinkedIn company 1128x191
                       Facebook 820x312 · X/Twitter 1500x500 · YouTube 2560x1440.

03_Social_Post_Templates/ → Ready branded backgrounds to post:
                       Instagram square 1080x1080 · portrait 1080x1350
                       Story/Reel/TikTok 1080x1920 · landscape 1200x675.

04_Web_App_Icons/    → Website + apps:
                       favicon.ico + favicon_16/32/48 = browser tab
                       AppleTouch_180 = iPhone home screen
                       PWA_192 / PWA_maskable_512 = installable web app
                       AppStore_1024 = App Store / Play Store listing
                       mark_transparent_1024 = icon with no background.

05_Logo_Lockups/     → The horizontal logo (icon + "QuotesDone"):
                       on_white / on_navy = ready backgrounds
                       OnLight/OnDark/Black_Mono _transparent = place anywhere
                       mark_only / mark_white = symbol on its own.

06_Print_Business_Card/ → 300 DPI, with bleed:
                       business_card_FRONT / BACK 1125x675 (edit the [ ] fields)
                       logo_horizontal_*_print = drop into letterhead, invoices, etc.

07_Trademark_and_License/ → Give these to the Ministry / IP agent / printer:
                       MARK_color_* and MARK_black_* (on white + transparent, 2000px)
                       LOCKUP_color/black_on_white  ·  BRAND_SQUARE_color_2000
                       Trademark filings usually want BOTH colour and black-and-white.
                       Trade-licence artwork: use BRAND_SQUARE or LOCKUP_color_on_white.

08_Vector_Source/    → Infinitely scalable (best for printers & IP filing):
                       mark_color/black/white .svg  ·  brand_square_bg .svg
                       mark_color.pdf · mark_black.pdf  (vector PDF).

TIP: For any official filing or a professional printer, send the 08_Vector_Source
files first — they never blur at any size.
'),
('cat:plumbing','Standards, materials & specifications',8,'Materials vocabulary: pressurised hot/cold water pipework is commonly PPR (polypropylene random copolymer) or CPVC, rated by PN class (nominal pressure in bar — e.g. PN16, PN20, PN25; higher PN = thicker wall/higher pressure and hot-water suitability); copper is used in some applications. Drainage/waste/soil uses uPVC. Fittings, mixers and sanitaryware should be from reputable brands; water heaters are specified by type (electric storage/instant) and capacity (e.g. 50/80/100 litres) and brands such as Ariston, Rheem, Bosch are common. Governing documents: the Dubai Building Code and DM Green Building Regulations & Specifications require water-efficient (low-flow) faucets, toilets and showers and, in qualifying buildings, greywater reuse and rainwater harvesting; DEWA guidelines cover supply and metering. Products are expected to meet UAE/Emirates conformity (ESMA/MOIAT) and recognised standards. Good-practice deliverables: correct pipe material and PN class for the duty, jointing per manufacturer method (heat-fusion for PPR, solvent-weld for CPVC/uPVC), supply pressure testing and drainage flow/leak testing, isolation valves and accessible cleanouts, and make-good of any opened surfaces. A method statement, fixture schedule (brand/model/capacity) and test certificate are the documents that make plumbing quotes comparable and verify quality.'),
('cat:curtains-blinds','Regulations, licensing & approvals',8,'Suppliers operate under a Dubai Department of Economy and Tourism (DET) trade licence (curtains/blinds trading or interior furnishing activity); free-zone licences exist but Dubai-mainland on-site installation generally needs a DET mainland licence. Fitting in occupied buildings: tenants usually need a landlord or owners-association NOC before drilling tracks, and community/master-developer rules (Emaar, Nakheel, Meraas, DAMAC) may apply. Fire-rated curtains and drapes in regulated occupancies (hotels, ballrooms, theatres, malls, offices, hospitals, schools) fall under the UAE Fire and Life Safety Code of Practice, administered by the General Command of Dubai Civil Defence (DCD); the consultant/contractor specifies FR-compliant fabrics and DCD reviews them as part of the building''s fire approval. For these projects the relevant control is the fabric''s FR test certificate accepted under the UAE Fire Code rather than a separate per-curtain DCD permit. Residential villa/apartment curtains have no fire approval requirement. Electrical connection for hard-wired motors should be done by a competent electrician; major new wiring in a villa may touch DEWA-registered contractor rules. Always confirm the supplier''s DET licence is valid and that any FR or hotel project explicitly references UAE Fire Code compliance and DCD acceptance, and that workmanship/warranty is in writing.'),
('cat:landscaping','Customer intake & scoping questions',9,'Ask: (1) Plot/garden area to be landscaped (sqm) and a site plan or photos? (2) Property type - villa, townhouse, apartment terrace, commercial/community - and is it owned or rented (NOC needed)? (3) Which community/developer (Emaar, Nakheel, Meraas, DAMAC, Trakhees/DDA) so we know the NOC and approval route? (4) What is the split you want - softscape (lawn, plants, trees), hardscape (paving, pergola, walls, lighting), or both? (5) Natural grass or artificial turf, and any specific plants/trees, theme, or low-water (xeriscape) preference? (6) Do you want an irrigation system - drip, pop-up sprinkler, or both - with a smart controller, and is the water source mains/sweet water or TSE? (7) Any structures - pergola/gazebo, deck, water feature, BBQ, pool surround - and approximate sizes (a pergola over ~20 sqm or 3 m high typically needs a permit)? (8) Outdoor lighting and power points required? (9) Existing drainage/slope issues, or need for retaining walls? (10) Is there site clearance/demolition or just a fresh build? (11) Do you want an ongoing garden maintenance contract after handover? (12) Timeline and any season constraints (summer heat affects planting)? (13) Budget range? (14) Will you handle NOC/permits or should we?'),
('_global','Asset text: README.txt',45,'From company asset "README.txt" (Dropbox: /QuotesDone Backup/Assets/QuotesDone_Corporate_Kit/README.txt)

