# QuotesDone — Engineering Backup — 2026-07-05

Author: management@doratajewelries.com · Kept for future reference / backup.

This folder preserves the durable (text) engineering artifacts from the 2026-07-05 session.
Binary code archives (the .zip snapshots) can''t be pushed through the Dropbox text-file API;
they live in the session outputs and should be mirrored via the Storage→Dropbox sync for a
true binary backup (see "Binary archives" below).

---

## 1. Greenfield NestJS backend ("marketplace execution engine")
A complete, compiling, tested NestJS 10 + Prisma 5 + PostgreSQL + Redis/BullMQ backend —
separate from the live Supabase system. Built and verified across 10 iterations (v2 → v10).

Final state (v10):
- 114 TypeScript source files; typecheck 0 errors; `nest build` → dist/src/main.js + dist/src/worker.js.
- Tests: 9 suites / 38 passing (unit + HTTP contract tests). E2E (full RFQ lifecycle) runs in CI.
- Capabilities: event-driven orchestrator (COO brain), guarded RFQ state machine, 6-factor
  matching, intent/pricing/supplier intelligence, AI memory graph, financial ledger (3% fee),
  immutable audit + AI-decision logs, field encryption (AES-256-GCM) + secrets abstraction,
  structured JSON logs (pino) + correlation IDs + OpenTelemetry tracing + Prometheus /metrics +
  Swagger /api/docs, 8 separated BullMQ queues + templated multi-channel notifications,
  TOTP MFA + WebAuthn passkeys + ABAC policy layer + admin IP allowlist,
  health/readiness probes, dedicated worker process.
- Ops: multi-stage Dockerfile, docker-compose full stack, CI (build/test + image build/push +
  compose smoke), raw Kubernetes manifests, and a Helm chart (helm lint 0 failures).
- Docs: versioned SRS under /docs (architecture, security, database, operations, deployment,
  ai-agents, knowledge-base, api, workflows).

Verification per pass: prisma validate/generate, tsc --noEmit (0), jest (green), nest build (ok),
helm lint/template (ok), docker compose smoke in CI.

## 2. Live CRM — Odoo-grade Pipeline Layer (deployed)
Deployed to Supabase project "suppliers DB" (htdblwldjkcgjvmqkbeh). Additive; existing crm_api
and Kanban untouched. See CRM_Pipeline_API.md (reference), CRM_Pipeline_deploy.sql (exact DDL),
and crm_pipeline_function.ts (exact edge-function source).
- New tables: crm_stages, crm_lost_reasons. New columns: inquiries.expected_value, .lost_reason.
- New views: crm_pipeline_report, crm_deal_kpis (RLS-locked).
- New edge function: crm_pipeline (stages_list, lost_reasons, pipeline_report, deal_update,
  activities_list, activity_add, activity_done).
- Verified: views return correct aggregates on live data; function ACTIVE; unauth → HTTP 403.

## Binary archives (NOT in this folder — action needed for true backup)
The full backend source is packaged as versioned zips in the session outputs:
`quotesdone-backend-v10-tests.zip` (latest, complete: 200 files incl. Helm/k8s/docs) plus
milestone zips v2→v9. To back these up in Dropbox as binaries, route them through the existing
Storage→Dropbox mirror (dropbox_sync). Ask in-session to wire that up.

## Convention (going forward)
Important artifacts to keep are stored under:
  /QuotesDone Backup/Assets/<Topic>_<YYYY-MM-DD>/
with a README.md manifest describing what each file is, its status, and how to restore it.
'),
('_global','Asset text: CRM_Pipeline_API.md',45,'From company asset "CRM_Pipeline_API.md" (Dropbox: /QuotesDone Backup/Assets/Engineering_Backend_Engine_2026-07-05/CRM_Pipeline_API.md)

# CRM — Odoo-grade Pipeline Layer (live)

Deployed to project **suppliers DB** (`htdblwldjkcgjvmqkbeh`). Additive — the existing
`crm_api` and Kanban (#272) are untouched. New endpoint: `functions/v1/crm_pipeline`
(same admin auth as crm_api: inbound `__secret` or admin-email + SMS-MFA session).

## What was added
**Structured stages** — `crm_stages` table: New(10%) · Qualifying(25%) · Matched(40%) ·
Quoted(60%) · Revealed(80%) · Won(100%) · Lost(0%) · Cancelled(0%), each with an ordered
position, win-probability, and won/lost flags. Existing deals (qualifying/revealed/lost)
map straight in.

**Deal economics** — `inquiries.expected_value` and `inquiries.lost_reason` columns, so the
pipeline carries money and closes with a reason.

**Lost reasons** — `crm_lost_reasons` table (Price too high, Chose a competitor, No budget,
Timing, No supplier response, Not qualified, Duplicate, Other).

**Analytics** — two views: `crm_pipeline_report` (per-stage deal count, total value,
probability-weighted value) and `crm_deal_kpis` (open/won/lost counts, avg sales-cycle days,
weighted forecast, overdue activities). RLS-locked (admin/service-role only).

**Activity management** — full API over the existing `crm_activities` table: schedule calls/
meetings/emails/todos with due dates, list them per record or as a global agenda, complete/
reopen, and a "next activity" rollup per record.

## Actions (POST JSON `{ action, ... }`)
| action | purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `stages_list` | ordered stages with probabilities |
| `lost_reasons` | active lost-reason picklist |
| `pipeline_report` | per-stage counts + value + weighted forecast, plus KPIs and win rate |
| `deal_update` | move a deal''s stage (auto-sets won→completed / lost→cancelled+reason), set `expected_value` / `deal_owner`; logs a stage-change activity |
| `activities_list` | activities for `{entity,entity_id}` (+ next_activity), or global open/overdue agenda |
| `activity_add` | schedule an activity (`type`, `subject`, `due_at`) on a record |
| `activity_done` | complete / reopen an activity |

## Verified
- Migration applied; `crm_pipeline_report` and `crm_deal_kpis` return correct aggregates
  against live data (qualifying 1 · revealed 1 · lost 2; open 2 / lost 2).
- Function deploys ACTIVE (Deno compiled) and guards correctly (unauthenticated → HTTP 403).
- New tables/views RLS-locked; grants revoked from anon/authenticated.

## Remaining polish (UI)
The `/crm` page already has the Kanban. To fully surface this: add a **Pipeline** panel that
calls `pipeline_report` (funnel + weighted forecast + win-rate cards), a **won/lost** control
on the deal drawer calling `deal_update`, and an **Activities** timeline calling the activity
actions. Backend is ready for all of it.
'),
('cat:plumbing','Authoritative sources & references',4,'Dubai Electricity and Water Authority (DEWA) — https://www.dewa.gov.ae/
DEWA Guidelines for New Development Projects — https://www.dewa.gov.ae/~/media/Guidelines_For_New_Dev_Projects_Issue_4_Update_2016.ashx
Dubai Municipality (Building Code, plumbing & drainage) — https://www.dm.gov.ae/
