('cat:curtains-blinds','Pricing benchmarks & red flags',7,'Indicative Dubai prices (verify; vary by fabric, size, brand): standard roller blinds from ~AED 149/sqm, blackout roller ~AED 199/sqm; motorised blinds from ~AED 399/sqm or a Somfy roller upgrade ~AED 220-280/sqm. Motorised curtains roughly AED 180-350/sqm depending on motor and fabric (battery from ~AED 180, wired from ~AED 200, smart-integrated from ~AED 250). Somfy motor installations indicatively AED 800-3,000 per motor by type/size; a Glydea/Irismo track-plus-motor package can run ~AED 1,000-2,000 on a standard 3x4m window including install. Drivers: fabric quality/gsm and brand, motor brand (genuine Somfy vs generic), window height (scaffolding for double-height), curved/bay tracks, FR-certified fabric premium, and quantity. Red flags: prices quoted only as vague per-sqm ''starting from'' with no fabric named; ''motorised'' without a motor brand/model (often a relabelled generic motor); blackout claimed but only dimout supplied; no FR certificate on a hotel/office job; supply-only price presented as installed; free measurement/install that inflates fabric price; missing 5% VAT; warranty on motor only (not fabric) or no written warranty; and refusal to provide the FR test certificate batch reference.'),
('cat:landscaping','Standards, materials & specifications',8,'Key authority documents: Dubai Municipality landscaping/horticulture guidelines and Local Order No. (8) of 2002 (sewerage, irrigation, drainage) governing irrigation and TSE reuse. Water sources: potable/sweet water (DEWA) vs TSE (treated sewage effluent) - TSE for unrestricted landscape irrigation must meet DM water-quality standards, run on dedicated purple/marked pipework, and include a backflow preventer; cross-connection with potable lines is prohibited. Irrigation types: drip/inline drip for shrubs and beds (water-efficient), pop-up spray/rotor sprinklers for lawns; smart controllers (e.g. Hunter, Rain Bird, Wi-Fi-based) with soil-moisture/rain sensors reduce waste and DEWA bills. Softscape vocabulary: topsoil and soil amendment, mulch, ground cover, sod/turf vs artificial grass (pile height mm, gsm, UV-stabilised for Gulf sun), plant grade/size (pot litres or height). Hardscape: interlock paving on compacted sub-base, natural stone, WPC/composite or aluminium pergola (wind-load rated), porcelain/travertine pool coping, retaining walls, low-voltage 12V garden lighting with transformer. Heat tolerance and salinity tolerance matter for plant selection in the UAE climate; native/adapted species (e.g. desert-adapted) lower water demand. Good specs name plant species and sizes, irrigation zones with backflow preventer and controller, soil depth, paving sub-base, and a plant-establishment/maintenance period.'),
('_global','Asset text: CHANGELOG.md',45,'From company asset "CHANGELOG.md" (Dropbox: /QuotesDone Backup/Assets/Engineering_Backend_Engine_2026-07-05/CHANGELOG.md)

# Changelog — CRM Pipeline layer

## 2026-07-06 — v3 (regression fix + Pipeline analytics UI)
Context: the 2026-07-05 deploy of `crm_pipeline` (v2) used new action names
(`deal_update`, `activities_list`) that did NOT match the action names the already-live
#272 CRM UI calls (`pipeline`, `deal_set_stage`, `activity_list`, `activity_add`). That
silently broke the Pipeline tab, the deal stage selector, and the activity timeline on the
live `/crm` page.

Fix (v3, deployed ACTIVE):
- `crm_pipeline` now supports BOTH contracts:
  - #272 UI: `pipeline` → `{board, kpis}`, `deal_set_stage`, `activity_list` → `{timeline}`, `activity_add`.
  - Analytics: `pipeline_report`, `stages_list`, `lost_reasons`, `deal_update`, `activities_list`, `activity_done`.
- The `pipeline` (Kanban) response now also returns `kpis` (open/won/lost, weighted forecast,
  win rate, avg cycle days, overdue activities).
- `/crm` page (`pages.slug=''crm''`): the Pipeline tab now renders a KPI cards strip above the
  Kanban (Weighted forecast · Open · Won · Lost · Win rate · Avg cycle · Overdue). Page
  auto-redeployed via the `mark_site_dirty` trigger.

Verified: function ACTIVE (Deno compiled); unauthenticated → HTTP 403; DB views return correct
aggregates; page injection confirmed (+866 bytes); deploy_state.dirty flipped true.

**The live deployed source is `crm_pipeline_function_CURRENT.ts` in this folder. The earlier
`crm_pipeline_function.ts` (v2) is superseded — do not redeploy it.**

Lesson recorded: before redeploying any live edge function, diff the existing action names
against every caller in the live pages/UI first.
'),
('_global','Asset text: README.md',45,'From company asset "README.md" (Dropbox: /QuotesDone Backup/Assets/Designer_Agent_2026-07-06/README.md)

# Designer Agent — AI image generation (status 2026-07-06)

## What it is
An in-house "Designer" agent that turns a short brief into an on-brand image (blog covers,
social posts, ad creatives), hosts it publicly, and saves it as a content draft.

## Components (all live in project htdblwldjkcgjvmqkbeh)
- **Edge function `designer` (v2, ACTIVE)** — image engine.
  - `POST {__secret, action:''generate'', prompt, purpose, size}` → OpenAI `gpt-image-1` →
    uploads PNG to the `brand` storage bucket → returns public `url`; also inserts a
    `content_drafts` row (channel=image, status=ready, source=agent:designer) and logs `agent_runs`.
  - `POST {__secret, action:''status''}` → readiness probe: `{ready, model, sizes, has_fallback, message}`.
  - Purposes → sizes: social/instagram/ad = 1024x1024; story/reel/portrait = 1024x1536;
    blog/linkedin/landscape = 1536x1024.
  - Brand guidance is pulled from `fn_agent_context(''designer'')` (see knowledge below).
  - Auth: `__secret == app_secrets.inbound_secret`.
- **Agent knowledge** — 4 rows under `agent_key=''designer''` (persona, brand_visual_system,
  capabilities, guardrails). See `designer_agent_knowledge.sql`.

## ⚠️ ACTION REQUIRED (founder-only) to activate
Image generation is dormant until the OpenAI key is set. In Supabase → project
htdblwldjkcgjvmqkbeh, add a secret row:
  `app_secrets.key = ''openai_api_key''`, `value = <your OpenAI API key>`
Until then, `generate` returns `{ok:false, ready:false, error:''openai_not_configured'', fallback_url}`
and `status` reports `ready:false`. No code change needed after the key is added.

## Verified
- Function ACTIVE (Deno compiled); unauthenticated → HTTP 403.
- Knowledge rows present (4). `default_post_image` fallback secret exists.
- Confirmed `openai_api_key` is NOT yet set (0 rows) — this is the only blocker.

## Not yet done (next deliberate step, optional)
- Agents-console UI trigger (a prompt box → calls `designer` → shows image + save).
- Secretary/Marketing auto-dispatch ("make a blog cover") → `designer`.
These touch large live functions + the /crm page; recommended as a separate, carefully-verified
change (avoid another hasty live edit). Backend is ready for both.
'),
('_global','Asset text: CRM_deal_drawer_2026-07-06.md',45,'From company asset "CRM_deal_drawer_2026-07-06.md" (Dropbox: /QuotesDone Backup/Assets/Engineering_Backend_Engine_2026-07-05/CRM_deal_drawer_2026-07-06.md)

# CRM deal drawer — expected value + lost reason (2026-07-06)

Live on `pages.slug=''crm''` (auto-deployed via the mark_site_dirty trigger; verified live on
quotesdone.com/crm, 58,379 bytes).

## What changed
The deal drawer''s `renderStageBar` was upgraded from a bare stage dropdown to a full
Odoo-style close control:
- **Expected value (AED)** number input — saves via `crm_pipeline` `deal_set_stage`
  `{inquiry_id, expected_value}` on change. This is what populates the Pipeline tab''s
  **weighted forecast** (value x stage probability).
- **Lost-reason picker** — when a deal is moved to `lost`/`cancelled`, a reason dropdown
  (loaded from `crm_pipeline` `lost_reasons`) appears; choosing a reason confirms the move
  via `deal_set_stage {inquiry_id, stage, lost_reason}` and logs a stage-change activity.
- Non-lost stage changes save immediately as before.

Signature change: `renderStageBar(id, cur)` -> `renderStageBar(id, cur, expVal)`; the caller
now passes `q.expected_value` from `deal_detail`.

Backend was already ready (deal_set_stage/deal_update accept expected_value + lost_reason;
lost_reasons action exists). No function redeploy needed for this UI increment.
'),
