# QuotesDone OS — Living Specification

This folder is the **single source of truth** for the QuotesDone platform. It is generated from a
direct audit of the live Supabase project (not from memory or chat history). If chat context is
ever lost, development can resume from these documents alone.

- **Project:** `htdblwldjkcgjvmqkbeh` ("suppliers DB"), region `ap-southeast-1`, Postgres 17.
- **Audit date:** 2026-07-06.
- **What it is:** A B2B construction/services procurement marketplace for the UAE (20k+ supplier
  directory) that has grown into an autonomous, AI-operated Company Operating System — CRM, ERP,
  knowledge platform, compliance engine, and a fleet of AI agents, all on one Postgres + Edge
  Function stack.

## Scale at a glance (live)

| Object | Count |
|---|---|
| Tables (public) | ~110, all RLS-enabled |
| Database functions | 289 (≈120 business `fn_*`/`trg_*`/`qd_*`/`run_*`, rest are pgvector/pg_trgm internals) |
| Views | 8 |
| Triggers | 43 |
| Cron jobs (pg_cron) | 62 |
| Edge Functions | 147 |
| AI category agents | 26 (one per trade) |
| Storage buckets | 11 |
| Roles | 9 (owner, admin, ops, finance, support, supplier, customer, agent, guest) |
| Frontend pages (in `pages` table) | 13 live (home, app, portal, crm, os, admin, about, legal, …) |
| Supplier directory (`leads`) | 20,467 |

## Documents

| File | Covers |
|---|---|
| `SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md` | Stack, layers, request lifecycle, page-as-module model, data flow |
| `DATABASE_SCHEMA.md` | Every table grouped by domain, key columns, relationships |
| `EDGE_FUNCTIONS.md` | All 147 Edge Functions grouped by domain, purpose, auth |
| `EDGE_FUNCTIONS_REFERENCE.md` | Complete per-function reference (~109 read at source): auth, actions, RPCs, integrations |
| `OPEN_ISSUES.md` | Findings from the source read: security gaps, data mismatches, consistency bugs (backlog) |
| `API_REFERENCE.md` | RPC functions (`fn_*`), `os_api` action protocol, edge endpoints |
| `AI_AGENTS.md` | The 26 category agents + executive/officer agents, memory, governance |
| `WORKFLOWS.md` | RFQ→quote→reveal→transaction, onboarding, disputes, approvals |
| `AUTOMATIONS.md` | All 62 cron jobs + 43 triggers and what they do |
| `SECURITY.md` | RLS model, roles/RBAC-ABAC, MFA, fraud, canaries, VirusTotal, PDPL |
| `KNOWLEDGE_PLATFORM.md` | KB chunks, regulations, MDM, playbooks, RAG, governance |
| `CRM.md` | Pipeline stages, deals, tasks, activities, notes, reporting |
| `ERP.md` | Finance snapshots, expenses, dues, invoices, reports |
| `MARKETPLACE.md` | Suppliers, RFQs, matching, quotes, pricing, reputation, twin |
| `REPORTING.md` | Board/exec/finance/monthly/quarterly reports, health index, analytics |
| `INTEGRATIONS.md` | Stripe, Twilio, Resend, Postiz, Dropbox, Gemini/OpenRouter, Apify, VirusTotal, Vercel, Meta, CloudConvert |
| `DEPLOYMENT.md` | Auto-deploy loop, Vercel, site publish, backups, DR drills |
| `FEATURE_INVENTORY.md` | Module completeness matrix / roadmap |
| `DECISIONS.md` | Architecture Decision Records (ADR-001…) |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | Reconstructed from 152 migrations + edge-fn versions |

## Living-spec rule (going forward)

Every change to the system **must** update the relevant document here in the same unit of work:

1. Schema change → `DATABASE_SCHEMA.md` (+ `CHANGELOG.md`).
2. New/changed Edge Function → `EDGE_FUNCTIONS.md` + `API_REFERENCE.md`.
3. New/changed RPC (`fn_*`) → `API_REFERENCE.md`.
4. New/changed AI agent, prompt, or governance rule → `AI_AGENTS.md`.
5. New/changed workflow, trigger, or cron → `WORKFLOWS.md` / `AUTOMATIONS.md`.
6. Any architectural decision → a new `ADR-###` in `DECISIONS.md`.
7. Always append a dated entry to `CHANGELOG.md`.

Documentation is part of the codebase, not an afterthought.
