# PENDING DEPLOY — Integrations Health panel (built 2026-07-06, awaiting Supabase)

Built during a Supabase-tooling outage (DB MCP returning 503). Deploy the moment it recovers.

## What this adds
A live **Integrations Health** check in the QuotesDone OS: pings every connected platform
server-side using the stored keys (the key never leaves the DB/edge function; only status returns)
and shows green / amber / red per provider, with the exact action needed for any red/amber.

Covers: **Stripe** (account + webhook endpoint + signing secret), **Resend** (domain verified),
**Twilio** (account + WhatsApp templates), **Meta** (access token), **OpenRouter**, **Vercel**,
**Apify**, **CloudConvert**, plus configured-status for **Postiz / Dropbox / Gemini / VirusTotal**,
and the platform config toggles (email/sms/whatsapp/marketing/invite/BD/supplier-email/TRN).

## Files (in this folder)
- `os_api_v3.ts` — the new `os_api` (v2 + a `health` action). Authoritative, clean.
- (page) — the `/os` command-center page with an "Integrations health" section + `Run check`
  button. Staged in the session outputs; re-verify before deploy (see step 2).

## Deploy steps (when Supabase MCP is back)
1. **Deploy the backend:** `deploy_edge_function` name `os_api`, `verify_jwt: true`, entrypoint
   `index.ts`, content = `os_api_v3.ts`. (Adds the `health` action; everything else unchanged.)
2. **Update the /os page:** take the edited command-center HTML (adds the Integrations section +
   `loadHealth()`), base64-encode it, and
   `update pages set html = convert_from(decode(''<b64>'',''base64''),''utf8''), updated_at=now()
    where slug=''os'';`  — first confirm the file contains `id=''ih_run''` and `loadHealth` and is
   ~16.5 KB (the sandbox copy was momentarily inconsistent during the outage; re-Read the
   file-tools version, or rebuild the two edits: an HTML `<div class=''sec''>Integrations health…`
   block after the attention queue, and a `loadHealth()` + `ihCard()` JS block after the
   `$(''refresh'').onclick` line).
3. **Verify live:** open `/os`, sign in as admin, click **Run check**. Or call `os_api {action:
   ''health''}` with an admin JWT and read the JSON.

## Then: the Stripe finding to action
The health check will confirm it, but from the stored config we already know:
- **`stripe_webhook_secret` is empty** → register a webhook at
  `https://htdblwldjkcgjvmqkbeh.supabase.co/functions/v1/stripe_webhook` for
  `checkout.session.completed`, then save its `whsec_…` via `/functions/v1/stripe_setup_page`.
- **`meta_access_token` missing** → ads can''t run; generate a Meta system-user token, save
  `meta_access_token`.
- **`company_trn` empty** → reveal invoices are receipts, not tax invoices (set if VAT-registered).

## Also pending from earlier
- Company OS **shell** rebuild (persistent app shell + workspaces) — `os_api` + `fn_ws_*` backend
  is already live; drop the leftover empty `pages._osb` column and redeploy the shell cleanly.
