# QuotesDone OS — Findings Report

Every finding carries evidence (file, line where useful), impact, and a recommended fix. "Fix applied" means fixed in the clean archive; anything touching production is **approval-gated** per the brief. Severity reflects business impact for an anonymous-marketplace product where supplier anonymity *is* the product (ADR-010).

---

## CRITICAL

### C1 — `v_supplier_billing` view is readable by `anon` and bypasses RLS: supplier identity leak
- **Evidence:** `database/schema.sql:23449–23496` — four views carry `GRANT ALL ... TO anon, authenticated` and are **not** `security_invoker`, so PostgREST executes them as owner, bypassing the deny-all RLS. `v_supplier_billing` selects `leads.company_name`, `leads.claimed_by AS email`, `founding_rank`, `banned`, `matching_blocked`, `subscription_paid_until` and subscription pricing from `app_secrets`.
- **Impact:** Anyone with the public anon key (embedded in every page, by design) can `GET /rest/v1/v_supplier_billing` and enumerate supplier identities, emails, and ban status — a direct violation of ADR-010 anonymity-by-construction, without any authentication. Siblings `v_llm_model_mix`, `v_llm_offpolicy` (internal LLM telemetry) and `v_kb_regulation_gaps` are exposed the same way.
- **Why it survived the 2026-07-07 hardening:** that pass fixed function grants and search_path but never inspected **view** grants.
- **Fix (production, ~5 min):** `REVOKE ALL ON v_supplier_billing, v_llm_model_mix, v_llm_offpolicy, v_kb_regulation_gaps FROM anon, authenticated;` then `ALTER VIEW ... SET (security_invoker = on);` for any view that should respect caller RLS. Edge functions use the service role and are unaffected. **Approval-gated but urgent.**

### C2 — `site_deploy` route map references two deleted functions; next deploy replaces the OS console with 404 bodies
- **Evidence:** `edge-functions/site_deploy/index.ts:44–45` — `MAIN[]` sources `BASE+''/os2''` and `BASE+''/os3''`; no `os2`/`os3` edge functions exist (189 dirs = 189 inventory rows; only `os_api`, `os_ops`, `os_pages` match `^os`). Line 242: `const html = await (await fetch(p.src)).text()` — **no `res.ok` check**; a Supabase 404 JSON body would be uploaded as `os3/index.html`. Cron: `site_autodeploy — * * * * *` and `auto_deploy — */2` (`database/cron-jobs.md:196`), dirty-flag driven (`mark_site_dirty` triggers, schema).
- **Impact:** On the next triggered deploy, `/os3` — and `/admin`, `/crm`, `/os2`, which redirect to it — serve an error body. The entire operator console disappears from the public site. (The console page row itself survives in the DB; this is a deploy-output corruption, recoverable but disruptive and confusing.)
- **Fix (production, small):** (a) point the two MAIN entries at a page-server for the `os3` row (or drop `/os2` from MAIN entirely and serve `/os3` via a generic pages renderer), and (b) add `if (!r.ok) throw` around every page fetch so a missing source aborts the deploy instead of shipping garbage. **Approval-gated; do this before anything marks the site dirty.**

### C3 — One shared secret grants unattended high-risk execution; static header bypass on the console gateway
- **Evidence:**
  - `edge-functions/secretary_act/index.ts:11–17` — any caller presenting `inbound_secret` is actor `''founder''`; the HIGH-risk tool set (`issue_refund`, `supplier_decision`, `delete_files`, `post_content`, mass `send_email`) pauses into `agent_pending_actions` but the **same caller can supply the confirm token** (`:184–193`). Admin-JWT path skips MFA (contrast `agent_act/index.ts:76`, which requires an MFA session).
  - `edge-functions/agent_act/index.ts:71,102–206` — `confirm` with `__secret` executes a **caller-supplied proposal** directly (no stored-proposal lookup, no MFA).
  - `edge-functions/os_api/index.ts:32–33` — `x-os-key` header equal to `app_secrets.os_bypass_key` substitutes for any JWT and any admin check (''os-preview@quotesdone.com'' identity); os_api then forwards chat to secretary_act with `inbound_secret` (`:69–73`), and secretary_act ignores the forwarded `actor_email`, so the command log attributes everything to "founder" — audit-trail loss.
  - `~128` functions gate on the **same** `inbound_secret` (grep `__secret` across edge-functions).
- **Impact:** A single leaked value (from a cron body, a log, a compromised integration) = refunds, supplier bans, file deletion, outbound mail, and admin data — with no second factor and a misattributed audit trail. This is the system''s single point of compromise, and it grows more dangerous as autonomy (ADR-016) expands.
- **Fix (production, staged):** (1) split secrets by risk domain (`cron_secret`, `console_secret`, `payments_secret`); (2) make `secretary_act` validate confirms only against **stored** `agent_pending_actions` created by a *different* actor, and record the real `actor_email`; (3) require MFA on the JWT path like `agent_act` does; (4) remove or rotate-per-session `os_bypass_key`. **Approval-gated.**

---

## HIGH

### H1 — Supplier quote-submission (text path) calls a deleted function → 404 in production
- **Evidence:** `pages/live/portal.html:102` (`aiQuote()` → `functions/v1/quote_ai`), call site `:205`. `quote_ai` is absent from the 2026-07-19 inventory; it is one of 10 functions still documented in `EDGE_FUNCTIONS.md` but no longer deployed. The file/image path uses `supplier_api` `extract_quote` and works.
- **Impact:** A supplier pasting quote text gets a silent failure — on the core marketplace loop, at the worst possible place (supplier''s first quote).
- **Fix:** Repoint the text path at the existing `supplier_api`/`quote_extract` action (or redeploy `quote_ai`). Requires editing the `pages.portal` row + redeploy. **Approval-gated.**

### H2 — `stripe_webhook_secret` (and `company_trn`) not set in production — payment webhook loop is dead until configured
- **Evidence:** `docs/dropbox-docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:28` (the newer variant of the doc): "Keys currently **not set**: `stripe_webhook_secret`, `company_trn`". `edge-functions/stripe_webhook/index.ts:43–44` fails closed (400 `not_configured`) when the secret is missing — correct behaviour, but it means every Stripe event is rejected.
- **Impact:** Reveal-fee and fine confirmations that arrive via webhook are dropped. Pre-launch (0 customers) this costs nothing yet — but it is a **launch blocker** and it also silently disables the "supplier cannot clear their own debt" server-side check noted at `stripe_webhook/index.ts:56`.
- **Fix:** Set the webhook signing secret in `app_secrets` (from Stripe dashboard) and fire a test event. 10 minutes. **Approval-gated (production secret).**

### H3 — 20 SECURITY DEFINER RPCs are EXECUTE-granted to `anon`
- **Evidence:** schema grants — callable unauthenticated via `/rest/v1/rpc/<fn>`: `fn_subscription_billing_run`, `fn_dropbox_list`, `fn_reconcile_licence_blocks`, `fn_supplier_stats`, `fn_customer_stats`, `fn_supplier_expiries`, `fn_expiring_docs`, `fn_sla_watch`, `fn_llm_drift_watch`, `fn_invite_week_activate`, `fn_policy_consistency_check`, `fn_protect_gate_secrets`, et al. The 2026-07-07 patch revoked only the `fn_os_*`/`fn_ws_*` set (verified applied).
- **Impact:** Owner-privileged, RLS-bypassing execution surface for unauthenticated callers — data disclosure (`fn_supplier_stats`) and state mutation (`fn_subscription_billing_run`, `fn_invite_week_activate`) depending on the function.
- **Fix (production, ~15 min):** extend the same `REVOKE EXECUTE ... FROM anon, authenticated, public` to this list. App calls them via service role — unaffected. **Approval-gated.**

### H4 — Blanket `anon` grants on 94 of 188 tables + `ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES` to anon: RLS is the only barrier
- **Evidence:** schema — `GRANT ALL ... TO anon` on 49 base tables, `SELECT` on 40 more, and default privileges granting future objects to anon automatically.
- **Impact:** '),
