# QuotesDone OS — Improvement Roadmap (prioritized)

Effort: S ≤ 1h · M ≤ 1 day · L = multi-day. Finding IDs reference `02_FINDINGS_REPORT.md`.
Everything below preserves existing functionality; no UI redesign, no new features, no business-logic change (per the brief). Items marked ⛔ block launch.

---

## P0 — This week (security + integrity emergencies)

| # | Action | Finding | Effort | Risk of doing it |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | ⛔ Revoke anon/authenticated on the 4 exposed views; set `security_invoker` | C1 | S | None — app uses service role |
| 2 | ⛔ Fix `site_deploy` MAIN (`os2`/`os3` entries) + add `res.ok` guard on page fetches | C2 | S | None — deploy aborts instead of shipping garbage |
| 3 | ⛔ Set `stripe_webhook_secret` in `app_secrets`; fire a Stripe test event; verify in `agent_runs` | H2 | S | None |
| 4 | Repoint portal paste-quote path from deleted `quote_ai` to `supplier_api extract_quote` (edit `pages.portal` + redeploy) | H1 | S–M | Low — mirror the working file path |
| 5 | Revoke anon EXECUTE on the 20 SECURITY DEFINER RPCs | H3 | S | None — service-role callers unaffected |
| 6 | Escape the ~6 unescaped console sinks (`crm_tasks.title`, error strings) in os3/portal/app rows | M1 | S | None |
| 7 | Export full `cron.schedule` definitions (secrets-scrubbed) into `database/cron-jobs.sql` | H8 | S | None — read-only |

**Exit criteria:** anonymous PostgREST returns zero rows/functions beyond `category_specs`; a dry-run `site_deploy` completes with every source `200 OK`; Stripe test event lands in `transactions`; portal text-quote path returns 200.

## P1 — Next 2 weeks (blast-radius reduction + AI reliability)

| # | Action | Finding | Effort |
|---|---|---|---|
| 8 | Split `inbound_secret` by domain (`cron_secret`, `console_secret`, `payments_secret`); rotate; keep the proven `agent_runs` verification pattern | C3 | M |
| 9 | `secretary_act`: confirm only **stored** pending actions created by a different actor; log real `actor_email`; require MFA on JWT path (pattern already exists in `agent_act:76`); remove or per-session-rotate `os_bypass_key` | C3 | M |
| 10 | `agent_act.confirm`: execute only proposals persisted by a prior `chat` turn (id lookup), never caller-supplied payloads | C3 | M |
| 11 | Email guardrails: recipient-domain allowlist for unattended sends; all external sends through pending-approval; delimit attachment text as data | H5 | M |
| 12 | Create `_shared/llm.ts` (models-array fallback, 1 retry + backoff, AbortController timeout, `llm_calls` telemetry, cached secret read) and migrate the 54 call sites mechanically | H9, M4 | L |
| 13 | Fix the 3 stale model chains now (one-liners) if #12 is scheduled later | M4 | S |
| 14 | Decide the prompt registry: wire `fn_prompt_get` into `inquiry_ai`/`quote_review` (with hardcoded fallback) **or** retire `prompt_gate`/`prompt_improve`/trainer branch. Recommendation: wire it — the eval infrastructure is already built and good | H7 | M |
| 15 | Remove default privileges / blanket grants to anon+authenticated; per-object grants only | H4 | M |

## P2 — This month (consolidation execution — needs your approval per item)

| # | Action | Finding | Effort |
|---|---|---|---|
| 16 | Delete 5 tombstone functions from the platform (`src_io`, `dev_login`, `qa_login`, `test_login`, `seed_asset` — all return 410 already) | L2 | S |
| 17 | 30-day invocation-log check on the 8 retired-console APIs (`admin_api`, `admin_detail`, `admin_insights`, `agent_brain`, `exec_board`, `ops_live`, `orchestrate`, `public_stats`) + legacy `secretary` v1 chat; then delete. `orchestrate` can go immediately (broken, H6) | L2, H6 | M |
| 18 | Prune `pages` table: 15 retired rows + unreachable `os` stub + unserved `setup-stripe` row (keep `legal_*_body` — live dependencies). Take a one-off backup first | L3 | S |
| 19 | Re-bake or runtime-load the Procurement Workspace so one copy exists (fixes stale labels users currently see) | M2 | M |
| 20 | Consolidate `asset_upload`/`asset_store`/`asset_put` into one allow-listed `asset_api`; update the few internal callers | M8 | M |
| 21 | Schema hygiene migration: HNSW on `leads.embedding_gte` (or drop it), PK on `rl_hits`, index `inquiries.parent_inquiry_id`, drop `idx_msg_inquiry`, drop `hlm_*` (3 tables, 0 rows) | M10, L8 | M |
| 22 | Pick one production deploy pipeline; demote `deploy_next_preview` to preview-only and re-enable Vercel deployment protection | M3 | M |
| 23 | Reconcile ADR-011 vs AUTONOMY_POLICY on auto-cleared high-risk kinds (relabel or stop auto-clearing) | M5 | S |
| 24 | Regenerate `EDGE_FUNCTIONS.md` from `_inventory.csv` + function headers (10 ghosts out, 60 missing in) | M11 | M |

## P3 — This quarter (structural durability)

| # | Action | Finding | Effort |
|---|---|---|---|
| 25 | Stand up a **git mirror** of production: nightly job exports functions + schema + cron + pages to a private repo. Keeps "production is truth" while ending "no history". This single change de-risks every future session | — | M |
| 26 | Add a drift gate: nightly Supabase advisors + grant-diff + view-grant check with founder alert (would have caught C1 the day it appeared) | C1/H4 | M |
| 27 | Honest-logging sweep: replace empty catches in the 57 functions with the `agent_runs` failure-counter pattern from `agent_autogen`/`learn_gaps`; fix `copilot` ok-on-fail and `email_triage` consume-on-fail | M6 | L |
| 28 | Consolidate 17 snapshot tables into partitioned `kpi_snapshots` | L9 | L |
| 29 | Single-source the agent roster + public pricing/policy facts (5 drifted roster copies; site_assistant FACTS vs support_ai FAQ) | AI-11 | M |
| 30 | Unify i18n: choose runtime-dictionary (already in app/portal) as the mechanism; fold `-ar` fork pages into it gradually; keep `qd_i18n` as the source | M2/frontend-7 | L |
| 31 | Cap prompt assembly in any retained chat agent; retire `agent_brain`/`secretary` v1 per #17 | M7 | S |
| 32 | Written conventions doc: naming (new objects), function template (gating, logging, secrets, CORS), "revoke-from-anon + invoker views + pinned search_path" defaults | L4 | S |

## Sequencing logic

P0 closes the three ways the current model is violated (C1/C2 + the broken flows) without touching architecture. P1 shrinks the blast radius of any single leaked value and makes the AI layer observable before autonomy expands (ADR-016 explicitly depends on this). P2 is the physical consolidation this audit was commissioned for — it is deliberately *after* the safety items because deleting legacy surfaces is only safe once logs prove silence. P3 buys durability: the git mirror (#25) and drift gate (#26) are the two highest-leverage changes on the whole list — they convert this audit from a snapshot into a standing guarantee.
